title: Yin-Yang Learner
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-10-21
authors:
  - family-names: Brisson
    given-names: Jean-François
    orcid: https://orcid.org/0009-0000-9778-5374
license: AGPL-3.0-only
repository-code: https://github.com/sparkainlp-x/yin-yang-learner
abstract: >-
  Two conjugate holographic membranes that crystallize by learning
  from each other's extracted patterns across an asymmetric
  predictive tic (yang reads yin's next-generation extraction).
  A measured negative result: the tic shortens the
  self-recreation horizon vs the symmetric baseline and the
  single-membrane control on all seeds tested, because the
  "predicted" state is a re-estimated state and the asymmetry
  compounds estimation error.
keywords:
  - holographic-memory
  - hebbian-learning
  - self-recreation
  - yin-yang
  - negative-result
